    // RAN: Review gate run 2026-11-10 for Sprint 4 (E3b e2eeClientFlows) on 70feb52, three passes per D0172 by two independent reviewer agents. Pass 1, the code review, found two High and five Medium findings. The switch dialog closed and re-opened itself around the create, so its own reload wiped the resolve step. The link's expected vault id was never scoped or cleared, so a stale link could block an unrelated vault. A cancel of the 409 modal left the create flow pending forever. A failed delete on an old server masked the cause. The Re-enrol action bypassed the link check. The join-by-name path swallowed failures. The delete raced the retry with a reconnect. Pass 2, the mechanism review against spec sections 4.4, 4.8, 4.9 and 6, found one High. The VaultGone re-create ran a plaintext create with no dialog on an unpinned name. The delete cleared the pin, so the pinned-name refusal did not bite after the migration delete. It found four Medium gaps. The define-off recoveries showed a Notice instead of a block. The Re-enrol flow, the modal reuse and the real 409 path had no test. It found two doc errors: the old-plugin card text and the pre-encryption backup advice. Pass 3, the clause check, marked clause 5 FAIL and clauses 1, 4, 8, 11 and 12 PASS-WITH-DEVIATION before the fixes. Every High and Medium finding is fixed in the closing commit. The pin survives the delete. A RecreateVaultModal opens on every VaultGone, pinned or not. The expected vid is keyed to the vault the link named. A fifth block reason E2eeLinkMismatch fails closed with no action. The define-off recoveries block with E2eeUnsupportedBuild. The conflict modal reports a cancel. The old-server delete is guarded. VK is zeroed on every exit. The switch dialog stays open. Tests pin each fix. The two Low findings that need another sprint are tracked. issue014 ties 1.33.0 to the first schema-4 tag. issue015 carries the D0108 share UI sentence. Two Low findings are accepted as named deviations in the task result. Re-enrol is a standalone join modal, and the login-password rule cannot run in token-only mode. Verdict PASS.
