    // RAN: Retro 2026-11-10 for Sprint 4 (E3b e2eeClientFlows). What the panel-fixed DoD got right: the thirteen clauses named every user surface. So the two reviewers could check each one against a test and found the gaps by clause. What the implementation changed: the pin now survives the delete, and the VaultGone recovery is a dialog in every case. A fifth block reason E2eeLinkMismatch exists, because a link check with a Re-enrol exit was the substitution the check refuses. The review found that the first cut had the plaintext re-create without a dialog and the stale link vid. Both are the class of defect a reviewer finds and a unit test did not. The first tests pinned the pure rules and the modals, not the plugin paths between them. The connect tests on the real plugin now pin those paths. Avoidable issues: none new in process terms. The RED-test convention of issue013 held, and the review found no secret leak. Already tracked: issue014 (the 1.33.0 tie, resolver e2eeRealServerE2e) and issue015 (the D0108 share UI sentence, resolver e2eeVaultKeyRotation), both under the tree of d0096. No new item: every follow-up is already tracked under d0096 as a task or an issue, so no backlog item is added. Wall time: about one sitting against the 5-point guideline of one day. The estimate held.
